    "body": "This isn't correct, at least as written. The conversion, presumably to an IDL `NotificationAction` type (although that isn't stated), will re-perform the Get()s of all the properties, which can be observable if Object.prototype is modified. Then we'll convert back to JS in the binding layer.\r\n\r\nI don't think there's any way to do this rigorously as long as your return type is `FrozenArray<NotificationAction>` (instead of `FrozenArray<object>`). The conversion between JS objects and dictionaries is observable and side effecting.",
